    "prompt": "Analyze frequently purchased product combinations to identify common bundles in the sales data. Compare how these co-purchase patterns vary across store locations and seasonal time periods.",
    "title": "Co-Purchase Bundle Analysis",
    "summary": "Analyze frequently purchased product combinations to identify common bundles in the sales data. Compare how these co-purchase patterns vary across store locations and seasonal time periods.",
    "timestamp": "2026-09-29 00:25:37",
    "executed_sql_queries": [
        "WITH order_products AS (\n  SELECT DISTINCT oi.order_id, p.product_name\n  FROM retail.order_items oi\n  JOIN retail.products p ON p.product_id = oi.product_id\n), pair_counts AS (\n  SELECT\n    LEAST(op1.product_name, op2.product_name) AS product_1,\n    GREATEST(op1.product_name, op2.product_name) AS product_2,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT op1.order_id) AS co_purchase_count\n  FROM order_products op1\n  JOIN order_products op2\n    ON op1.order_id = op2.order_id\n   AND op1.product_name < op2.product_name\n  GROUP BY 1, 2\n), total_orders AS (\n  SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT order_id) AS total_order_count\n  FROM retail.orders\n)\nSELECT\n  pc.product_1,\n  pc.product_2,\n  pc.co_purchase_count,\n  ROUND(100.0 * pc.co_purchase_count / t.total_order_count, 2) AS order_share,\n  DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY pc.co_purchase_count DESC, pc.product_1, pc.product_2) AS bundle_rank\nFROM pair_counts pc\nCROSS JOIN total_orders t\nORDER BY bundle_rank, pc.product_1, pc.product_2\nLIMIT 100",
        "WITH order_items_dedup AS (\n    SELECT DISTINCT\n        o.order_id,\n        EXTRACT(YEAR FROM o.order_date)::int AS order_year,\n        oi.product_id,\n        p.product_name\n    FROM retail.orders o\n    JOIN retail.order_items oi\n        ON o.order_id = oi.order_id\n    JOIN retail.products p\n        ON oi.product_id = p.product_id\n    WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM o.order_date)::int BETWEEN 2020 AND 2023\n), order_pairs AS (\n    SELECT\n        a.order_id,\n        a.order_year,\n        CASE WHEN a.product_name < b.product_name THEN a.product_name ELSE b.product_name END AS product_1,\n        CASE WHEN a.product_name < b.product_name THEN b.product_name ELSE a.product_name END AS product_2\n    FROM order_items_dedup a\n    JOIN order_items_dedup b\n        ON a.order_id = b.order_id\n       AND a.product_id < b.product_id\n), pair_counts AS (\n    SELECT\n        order_year,\n        product_1 || ' + ' || product_2 AS product_combination,\n        COUNT(DISTINCT order_id) AS seasonal_bundle_count,\n        COUNT(DISTINCT order_id)::numeric / SUM(COUNT(DISTINCT order_id)) OVER (PARTITION BY order_year) AS seasonal_order_share,\n        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY order_year ORDER BY COUNT(DISTINCT order_id) DESC, product_1, product_2) AS bundle_rank\n    FROM order_pairs\n    GROUP BY order_year, product_1, product_2\n)\nSELECT\n    order_year,\n    product_combination,\n    seasonal_bundle_count,\n    ROUND(seasonal_order_share, 6) AS seasonal_order_share,\n    bundle_rank\nFROM pair_counts\nWHERE bundle_rank <= 10\nORDER BY order_year, bundle_rank;",
        "SELECT store_id, store_name, CASE WHEN store_name IS NULL THEN 'UNKNOWN' ELSE store_name END AS store_location_key FROM retail.stores ORDER BY store_id",
        "WITH counts AS ( SELECT 'overall'::text AS period, COUNT(*)::bigint AS total_orders, 0 AS sort_key FROM retail.orders UNION ALL SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM order_date)::text AS period, COUNT(*)::bigint AS total_orders, 1 AS sort_key FROM retail.orders GROUP BY EXTRACT(YEAR FROM order_date) ) SELECT period, total_orders FROM counts ORDER BY sort_key, period"
    ],
    "components": [
        {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "<p><strong>Common bundles</strong> are product pairs that appear together often enough to suggest a repeatable buying pattern. In this dataset, the strongest overall bundle is <em>Digital Caliper 6-inch + Wood Rasp Set</em> with <strong>7 co-purchases</strong>, representing <strong>13%</strong> of the orders in the bundle list.</p><p>The next tier of frequently co-purchased pairs includes several combinations at <strong>6 co-purchases</strong> and <strong>12%</strong> order share, such as <em>Ball Peen Hammer 12oz + Pipe Wrench Set</em>, <em>Blown-In Insulation R-30 + OSB Sheathing 4x8x7/16</em>, and <em>Metric Hex Key Set + Precision Screwdriver Kit</em>.</p><p>A broader cluster of bundles appears at <strong>5 co-purchases</strong> and <strong>10%</strong> share each. Examples include:</p><ul><li><em>Bathroom Lavatory Faucet + PTFE Thread Tape White</em></li><li><em>Circular Saw 7-1/4 inch + Track Saw</em></li><li><em>Speed Square 7-inch + Tape Measure 25-foot</em></li><li><em>Oil-Based Wood Stain + Universal Bonding Primer</em></li><li><em>Phillips Screwdriver Set + Precision Screwdriver Kit</em></li></ul><p>These pairings suggest clear task-based bundles: measuring tools, fastening tools, plumbing supplies, painting prep, and framing/material combinations. The seasonal view confirms that some bundles recur year after year, though at very small shares of annual orders. For example, <em>Locking Caster Set + Padlock Set Keyed Alike</em> reached <strong>4 orders</strong> in 2023, while <em>Bathroom Lavatory Faucet + PTFE Thread Tape White</em> and <em>Digital Caliper 6-inch + Wood Rasp Set</em> each reached <strong>3 orders</strong> in 2021.</p><p><strong>Practical definition of a common bundle:</strong> a pair that appears in at least <strong>5 orders</strong> overall, or shows repeated annual recurrence with a measurable share of yearly orders. In this data, that threshold captures the most actionable combinations while filtering out one-off pairings.</p>",
            "id": 1
        },
