            "type": "text",
            "content": "<p><strong>Key bundle patterns</strong> show a mix of <em>tool-to-tool</em>, <em>project-material</em>, and <em>garden/home-improvement</em> pairings. The top bundle is <strong>Digital Caliper 6-inch + Wood Rasp Set</strong> with <strong>7 co-purchases</strong>, representing <strong>13%</strong> of the top-bundle set. Two bundles tie next at <strong>6 co-purchases</strong> each (<strong>12%</strong>): <strong>Ball Peen Hammer 12oz + Pipe Wrench Set</strong>, <strong>Blown-In Insulation R-30 + OSB Sheathing 4x8x7/16</strong>, and <strong>Metric Hex Key Set + Precision Screwdriver Kit</strong>.</p><p><strong>Cross-category behavior is strong</strong>: many high-frequency pairs combine complementary items rather than identical products. Examples include <strong>Bathroom Lavatory Faucet + PTFE Thread Tape White</strong>, <strong>Speed Square 7-inch + Tape Measure 25-foot</strong>, and <strong>Oil-Based Wood Stain + Universal Bonding Primer</strong>. This suggests customers often bundle items needed to complete a single task in one trip.</p><p><strong>Seasonal shifts are notable.</strong> In <strong>2020</strong>, the leading seasonal bundles were mostly power-tool and construction combinations, each appearing <strong>2 times</strong> with a <strong>0.1712% order share</strong>. By <strong>2021</strong>, plumbing and precision-tool bundles became more prominent, led by <strong>Bathroom Lavatory Faucet + PTFE Thread Tape White</strong>, <strong>Coping Saw + Ratcheting Screwdriver</strong>, and <strong>Digital Caliper 6-inch + Wood Rasp Set</strong>, each at <strong>3 orders</strong> and <strong>0.2760%</strong> share.</p><p>In <strong>2022</strong>, organizational and hand-tool pairings rose, especially <strong>Heavy Duty Wall Hook Set + Pegboard Tool Holder Set</strong> and <strong>Lineman's Pliers 9-inch + Needle-Nose Pliers 6-inch</strong>, both at <strong>3 orders</strong> and <strong>0.2244%</strong> share. In <strong>2023</strong>, the standout bundle was <strong>Locking Caster Set + Padlock Set Keyed Alike</strong> with <strong>4 orders</strong> and the highest seasonal share at <strong>0.3257%</strong>, indicating a shift toward storage/security-related purchases.</p><p><strong>Interpretation:</strong> bundle behavior appears to evolve from <em>construction and power tools</em> in earlier periods toward <em>plumbing, organization, and security/storage</em> in later periods. The recurring presence of measurement, fastening, and finishing tools across the top bundles suggests customers are increasingly buying <strong>task-complete kits</strong> rather than isolated items.</p>",
